<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ruby on Oshan Wisumperuma</title><link>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/tags/ruby/</link><description>Recent content in Ruby on Oshan Wisumperuma</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:52:22 +1000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://oshanwisumperuma.com/tags/ruby/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Functional Ruby</title><link>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/functional-ruby/</link><pubDate>Thu, 31 Jan 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/functional-ruby/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="featured-Screenshot-from-2019-01-31-11-32-10.png" alt="&amp;quot;&amp;quot;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Eigenclass in Ruby</title><link>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/2016-04-08-eigenclass/</link><pubDate>Fri, 08 Apr 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/2016-04-08-eigenclass/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;References:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.integralist.co.uk/posts/eigenclass.html"&gt;http://www.integralist.co.uk/posts/eigenclass.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gist.github.com/Integralist/bb8760d11a03c88da151"&gt;https://gist.github.com/Integralist/bb8760d11a03c88da151&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;When creating singleton methods (i.e. &lt;code&gt;def self.foo&lt;/code&gt;), Ruby creates an anonymous class to hold them. This anonymous class — the eigenclass — assumes the role of the object&amp;rsquo;s class, and the original class is re-designated as its superclass.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; is actually a method.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;private&lt;/code&gt; method only changes the visibility of instance methods.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Class methods, on the other hand, are instance methods of the eigenclass.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Test&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;bar&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;puts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;bar&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;foo&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;puts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;foo&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;private_class_method&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;:foo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;:bar&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bar&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;Test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;foo&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ampersand Operator in Ruby</title><link>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/2016-04-04-ampersand-operator/</link><pubDate>Mon, 04 Apr 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://oshanwisumperuma.com/posts/2016-04-04-ampersand-operator/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s how a function call with an ampersand looks:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;some_function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;an_object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;When used like this, the &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; operator calls &lt;code&gt;to_proc&lt;/code&gt; on the argument and passes the resulting &lt;code&gt;Proc&lt;/code&gt; object (explained below) as a block to the method.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="whats-a-proc"&gt;What&amp;rsquo;s a Proc?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;code&gt;Proc&lt;/code&gt; object encapsulates a function or a block in a way that can be passed around as a variable. We can initialize one with a block like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ruby" data-lang="ruby"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;Proc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then use the &lt;code&gt;call&lt;/code&gt; method to invoke it:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>